        "source_title": "World Bank press release, 17 April 2024",
        "source_quote": "issued three catastrophe (cat) bonds that finance $420 million of insurance coverage for the Government of Mexico against named storm events along the Atlantic coast of Mexico and earthquake events.",
        "secondary_source_url": "https://thedocs.worldbank.org/en/doc/8f7222d60ec54d0b6571131b754319c1-0340012025/original/Case-Study-Mexico-2024-Cat-Bond.pdf",
        "secondary_source_title": "World Bank case study, 27 February 2025",
        "secondary_source_quote": "the World Bank issued 4 catastrophe (cat) bonds that provide the Government of Mexico with $295 million financial protection against earthquakes and $300 million against named storms.",
        "geometry_source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/johan/world.geo.json/master/countries/MEX.geo.json",
        "geometry_note": "Simplified Mexico country outline (d). Vertex coordinates come from the public simplified country boundary at geometry_source_url (a commonly used public GeoJSON of Mexico), not from the prospectus. The World Bank press release and case study identify the coverage as being for Mexico / the Government of Mexico against earthquake events; they do not publish a polygon or any other region description beyond Mexico. This outline is not a contractual coverage area and not a contractual coverage box. Those deal geometries are not published on this site.",
        "note": "Outline is a simplified Mexico country outline for display, not the bond's contractual covered area. Contract tests are not shown publicly.",
        "public_basis": "World Bank press release, 17 April 2024, and World Bank case study, 27 February 2025: coverage for the Government of Mexico against earthquake events. Geometry is a simplified country outline (d), not a contractual coverage area or box.",
